course: dictionary
lesson: 2631
title: Desperate: more than sad
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: The word desperate can mean very different things, so the context tells you which one. Ask yourself: is someone hoping hard against the odds, or is the thing very serious? «A desperate attempt» is a last try with little chance of success, while «desperate for a drink» means wanting something very much.
explain: When someone feels desperate, they have little hope and will do almost anything to change things. Stories use this feeling: desperate characters take risks, so «a desperate situation» is one full of danger. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still fits.
explain: In everyday talk the word is lighter. People say «desperate to go» or «desperate for the loo» to mean they badly want something, and «gasping» means desperate for a drink. The same word can be serious or silly, so always read the clues around it.
fact: Desperate is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «a desperate attempt».
fact: Desperate means feeling that you have little hope and will do anything to change the situation.
fact: «Desperate for» and «desperate to» mean wanting something very much.
fact: «Desperate measures» are extreme actions taken as a last try, as in «desperate times call for desperate measures».
fact: Desperate is on the Years 5–6 list of harder words in England, so you will meet it often in reading and writing.
exercise: In «desperate for a drink», what does desperate mean? | Very dangerous | Full of hope and calm | Neat and tidy | *Wanting something very much
exercise: Which phrase shows a very serious or dangerous time? | donkey's years | our kid | *a desperate situation | a cuppa
exercise: In «desperate for the loo», what does desperate mean? | Very neat and tidy | Standing in a dangerous place | Feeling sleepy and tired | *Needing the toilet very badly
test: In «desperate times call for desperate measures», what are desperate measures? | Small and careful steps | Measures of length, like inches | Happy and cheerful plans | *Extreme actions taken as a last try
test: Which feeling does desperate describe? | Bored of waiting for something | Fizzy and bubbly | Very calm and relaxed | *Little hope, and willing to do anything to change things
exam: Dev says desperate just means sad. Is he right? | *No, it can mean wanting something very much, a dangerous situation, or a last try | Yes, it only means happy | Yes, it means exactly the same as sad | No, it means very quiet
